<p>
  <b>{$summary}</b> - {$verdict}
</p>

<p>
  Every test here is an ordinary page, fetched over HTTP with
  <code>&amp;padInclude</code> so it renders bare, and compared with the outcome written beside
  it, exactly as in the <a href="?pages/index">Pages</a> suite. The difference is what the page
  is allowed to reach: these tests live in <code>apps/regression/common/</code>, where
  <code>_common</code> is on, because they use it - <code>{ignore}{example}{/ignore}</code>,
  <code>{ignore}{demo}{/ignore}</code>, <code>{ignore}{table}{/ignore}</code>, the
  <code>{ignore}{block}{/ignore}</code> snippet, the colouring functions in
  <code>_common/_lib/</code>. <code>show</code> is the crawl's own view of a test - what it
  renders now against the copy the last crawl stored.
</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0">
  <tr><th>page</th><th>what it checks</th><th>show</th><th>status</th></tr>
  {tests}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{$url}">{$name}</a></td>
      <td>{echo $what | ignore}</td>
      <td><a href="{$show}">show</a></td>
      <td>{$status}</td>
    </tr>
  {/tests}
</table>